<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · period</p><h1 class="enc-title">Carolingian Renaissance</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Carolingian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/renaissance">Renaissance</a> was a revival of learning, literature and the arts in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carolingian-empire">Carolingian Empire</a> in the late eighth and ninth centuries. Led by scholars such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alcuin-of-york">Alcuin</a> at the court of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charlemagne">Charlemagne</a>, it promoted education, church reform and the copying of classical and Christian texts. Many ancient <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> works survive because they were preserved in this period.</p></div>
